ef 17592186045417] [17592186546967 #edb/ref 1071 "Evaluate the limit:\n\n${lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\,\\,\\frac{6{x}^{7}-3{x}^{3}-4}{2{x}^{5}+7}=$\n\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186546967 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "1544d2ec-f693-56d4-9990-975c61a78ee3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186546967 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we divide both the numerator and the denominator by the highest power of $x$ in the denominator, which is ${x}^{5}.$ Then, by noting that the reciprocals shrink to $0$ in the limit, we can then evaluate the resulting expression.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\,\\,\\frac{6{x}^{7}-3{x}^{3}-4}{2{x}^{5}+7} & ={lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\,\\,\\frac{(\\frac{6{x}^{7}}{{x}^{5}}-\\frac{3{x}^{3}}{{x}^{5}}-\\frac{4}{{x}^{5}})}{(\\frac{2{x}^{5}}{{x}^{5}}+\\frac{7}{{x}^{5}})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\,\\,\\frac{(6{x}^{2}-\\frac{3}{{x}^{2}}-\\frac{4}{{x}^{3}})}{(2+\\frac{7}{{x}^{5}})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\,\\,\\frac{6{x}^{2}-0-0}{2+0} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }3{x}^{2} \\\\  & =\\infty .\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547096 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186547161 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547096 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "22c02e95-1ba7-5783-9176-80a1df536b87" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547096 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186323718 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547134 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "a143b3fe-a7b0-5158-a0a9-b332fd420167" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547134 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186546967 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547148 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186547096 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547148 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "c6ad608c-1279-5180-92ac-08be742f15d5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547148 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186124911 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547154 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186547134 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547154 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "d1b2f87b-6dcc-5404-a314-4a4505ca7a2d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547154 #edb/ref 1063 #ed